as played a significant role in advancing digital banking solutions, including the introduction of mobile banking applications. In 2011, the bank launched its mobile banking services, marking a significant step in enhancing customer convenience and accessibility to banking services.\n\nIn addition to its mobile banking applications, Pekao SA has also been a pioneer in mobile payment systems. The bank introduced PeoPay, a mobile payment solution that allows customers to conduct transactions seamlessly through their mobile devices. This innovation reflects Pekao SA's commitment to integrating cutting-edge technology into its services to meet the evolving needs of its customers.\n\nPekao SA is part of Group 3, which includes banks characterized by an average level of mobile banking adoption among their customers. This indicates that while Pekao SA has made significant strides in offering mobile banking solutions, there is still room for growth in terms of customer adoption and engagement with these digital services.\n\nOverall, Pekao SA's efforts in mobile banking and payment systems underscore its position as a leading bank in Poland, dedicated to providing modern and efficient banking solutions to its clientele.", "BANK BPH:Bank BPH is a Polish bank that was among the financial institutions offering mobile banking applications in Poland starting in 2012.", "BANK NORDEA:Bank Nordea is a Polish bank that played a significant role in the early adoption of mobile banking applications in Poland. Starting in 2012, the bank began offering mobile banking applications, marking a pivotal step in modernizing banking services in the region. Through its innovative approach, Bank Nordea contributed to the transformation of the banking landscape in Poland by providing customers with convenient and accessible financial services via mobile platforms.", "ALIOR SYNC:Alior Sync is a digital banking service that was launched by Alior Bank in 2012. It played a significant role in the early stages of mobile banking in Poland. As a pioneering initiative, Alior Sync provided mobile banking applications that allowed users to manage their finances conveniently through their smartphones. Over time, Alior Sync became an integral part of Alior Bank, contributing to the bank's reputation as an innovator in the digital banking sector.", "ING BANK ŚLĄSKI:ING Bank Śląski is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its leadership in mobile banking services. Established as one of the top five banks in the country by client numbers, ING Bank Śląski has consistently demonstrated innovation in the digital banking sector. The bank was a pioneer in offering mobile banking applications, launching its first app in 2012. It was notably the first Polish bank to introduce a mobile banking application specifically designed for tablets, showcasing its commitment to technological advancement and customer convenience.\n\nA key player in the development of mobile payment systems, ING Bank Śląski was one of the six banks involved in the creation of the BLIK payment system, which has become a widely used service in Poland. Since 2015, the bank has been providing BLIK services to its customers, enabling them to perform contactless payments and other functionalities with ease. In addition to BLIK, ING Bank Śląski offers a range of mobile payment options, including HCE, Google Pay, Apple Pay, and Garmin Pay, catering to the diverse needs of its tech-savvy clientele.\n\nThe bank's involvement in the Polish Standard of Payments further underscores its role in shaping the country's digital payment landscape. With a significant number of mobile banking users and high mobilization indicators, ING Bank Śląski continues to lead in the adoption and implementation of cutting-edge banking technologies. Its comprehensive suite of mobile banking services not only enhances customer experience but also solidifies its position as a forward-thinking institution in the competitive Polish banking market.", "GETIN BANK:Getin Bank is a prominent financial institution based in Poland, known for its innovative approach to mobile banking and payment solutions. Since the launch of its mobile banking applications in 2013, Getin Bank has continuously expanded its digital services to meet the evolving needs of its customers. The bank offers a variety of secure mobile banking login methods, including traditional password entry, graphic sign, PIN, fingerprint recognition, and face scan technology, ensuring a high level of security and convenience for its users.\n\nIn addition to its robust mobile banking platform, Getin Bank provides a comprehensive suite of mobile payment options. Since 2016, the bank has been offering BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland that allows users to make quick and secure transactions using their smartphones. Furthermore, Getin Bank supports a range of other mobile payment systems, including Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, and Xiaomi Pay, enabling customers to choose the payment method that best suits their lifestyle and preferences.\n\nThrough its commitment to technological advancement and customer-centric services, Getin Bank has established itself as a leader in the Polish banking sector, offering a seamless and secure banking experience to its clients.", "EUROBANK:Eurobank is a Polish bank that began offering mobile banking applications in 2013. As one of the banks in Poland to provide such services at that time, Eurobank played a role in the early adoption of mobile banking technology within the country.", "BNP PARIBAS:BNP Paribas is a prominent financial institution operating in Poland, recognized for its comprehensive suite of mobile banking services. The bank has been at the forefront of mobile banking innovation, having introduced mobile banking applications as early as 2013. BNP Paribas offers a wide array of mobile payment systems, including BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, Fitbit Pay, Swatch PAY!, and Xiaomi Pay, catering to the diverse needs of its customers.\n\nDespite its extensive offerings, BNP Paribas has been noted for having lower than average mobile banking indicators within the Polish market. However, it is part of a larger group that boasts a high percentage of 'mobile only' users, indicating a strong focus on digital banking solutions. The bank's commitment to mobile banking is further evidenced by its participation in the development of mobile banking applications in Poland, highlighting its role in advancing the country's digital banking landscape.\n\nBNP Paribas has been providing BLIK services since 2017, further enhancing its mobile payment capabilities. As a global bank, BNP Paribas leverages its international expertise to deliver robust mobile banking services in Poland, positioning itself as a leading bank in the region. Through its diverse range of mobile payment options and continuous innovation in mobile banking, BNP Paribas remains a key player in Poland's financial sector, dedicated to meeting the evolving needs of its customers.", "PKO BP:PKO BP, also known as IKO, is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its extensive mobile banking services. As one of the six banks involved in the creation of the BLIK payment system, PKO BP has been offering BLIK services since 2015, which include contactless payments and other functionalities. The bank is a key player in the Polish Standard of Payments and has introduced the IKO mobile payment system, further solidifying its position in the mobile banking sector.\n\nWith a strong focus on digital innovation, PKO BP has developed a robust mobile banking platform that caters to a large customer base. The bank boasts 3.91 million active mobile app users and serves a total of 10.54 million individual clients. This highlights its significant presence in the Polish banking industry and its commitment to providing convenient and efficient banking solutions to its customers.\n\nPKO BP's mobile application usage metrics have been analyzed, indicating its role as a major bank in Poland with moderate mobile banking indicators. The bank's mobile services are well-regarded, and it continues to enhance its offerings to meet the evolving needs of its clients. As a leading bank in Poland, PKO BP remains dedicated to delivering high-quality financial services and maintaining its reputation as a trusted and innovative banking institution.", "POLSKI STANDARD PŁATNOŚCI:Polski Standard Płatności is a company that was established in 2013 by a consortium of six banks with the primary objective of managing and coordinating the development of the BLIK mobile payment system in Poland. As the entity responsible for overseeing the BLIK project, Polski Standard Płatności plays a crucial role in the advancement and management of this innovative payment system within the country. The BLIK system, under the stewardship of Polski Standard Płatności, has become a significant player in the Polish financial landscape, offering a convenient and secure mobile payment solution to users. Through its efforts, Polski Standard Płatności continues to enhance the functionality and reach of BLIK, ensuring it meets the evolving needs of consumers and remains at the forefront of mobile payment technology in Poland.", "SGB MOBILE:SGB Mobile is a mobile banking application for clients of the SGB Cooperative Banking Group, launched in July 2020", "GOOGLE PAY:Google Pay is a mobile payment system that began its operations in Poland in November 2016. It is widely available across many banks in the country, providing users with a convenient and secure method for making payments using their mobile devices. This service allows users to store their credit and debit card information on their smartphones, enabling them to make contactless payments at various retail locations. By integrating with numerous banking institutions, Google Pay has established itself as a versatile and accessible payment solution for Polish consumers, enhancing the ease of financial transactions in the region.", "GARMIN PAY:GARMIN PAY is a mobile payment system that has been available in Poland since March 2018. It allows users to make payments conveniently through their smartwatches. The service is supported by many banks in Poland, making it widely accessible to users who wish to utilize their Garmin smartwatches for contactless payments. This integration of technology and finance provides a seamless and efficient payment solution for those who prefer using wearable devices for their transactions.", "FITBIT PAY:FITBIT PAY is a mobile payment system that was launched in October 2018. It is designed to cater to active individuals and athletes, providing them with a convenient and secure way to make payments on the go. The system is available through select banks in Poland, allowing users to link their bank accounts to their Fitbit devices. This integration enables users to make contactless payments directly from their Fitbit smartwatches or fitness trackers, eliminating the need to carry cash or cards during workouts or daily activities. By focusing on the needs of active users, FITBIT PAY offers a seamless payment experience that aligns with the lifestyle of its target audience.", "SWATCHPAY:SwatchPay is a mobile payment system launched in December 2020, designed for use with Swatch watches", "XIAOMI PAY:Xiaomi Pay is a mobile payment system that was launched in October 2021. It is available in Poland through several banks, including Bank Pocztowy, SGB, and mBank. This service allows users to make payments using their mobile devices, providing a convenient and modern alternative to traditional payment methods. Xiaomi Pay's integration with these banks enables customers to easily manage their transactions and finances through their smartphones, enhancing the overall banking experience."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_e3cd8c